NoteAbout this page



This page tests panzoom’s match: auto mode. The markup is identical to a-lightbox (no panzoom markers at all); both panzoom: match: auto and lightbox: match: auto are on. panzoom should take every image that Quarto’s auto lightbox would take, except where a case asks for something explicit:

cases 6 and 7 set #| lightbox: options, so they stay with GLightbox;
case 8 sets #| lightbox: false, so it gets neither;
case 9 (image inside a link) and case 11 (inline image) are skipped, as Quarto’s auto mode skips them.

Compare each case with the same numbered case in a-lightbox.

NoteAbout this page



This page tests very wide and tall figures in galleries and layouts: collages (25 × 2 inches) and tall strips grouped into galleries, as subfigures and in a layout div. The same shapes on their own, and the fit option, are on H: wide and tall figures.
Wide figures open at screen height from the left end, tall ones at screen width from the top. Headings carry expect-fit, the way each image should open. On the galleries, the browser test also checks that Left/Right pan (or, on a tall strip, do nothing) rather than switch, and that the previous and next buttons switch.
The cases below draw with these helpers:
```{r}
# A collage: `n` panels side by side, like a wide patchwork figure.
